{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1188924-please-help-me-understand-injury-conditions","id":1188924,"title":"Please Help Me Understand Injury Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-23T10:39:24-08:00","id":1188924,"title":"Please Help Me Understand Injury Conditions","content":"When do you apply Bruised Ribs -1 Defense or Cracked Ribs -2 Defense or Black Eyes Increase Difficulty of Aim Action...<br /> <br /> I believe I read a section that said when you are Bruised -1 you have to overcome a complication for every action and when you are Injured -2 you have to overcome 2 complications for every action... etc. If that is true when I am Bruised with a -1 complication do I also have a black eye fudging my aim?<br /> <br /> Do they not stack. Have I got it all completely wrong?<br /> <br /> Under the Shot Caller Gift it says: &quot;(See p. XX for list of Injury Condition and how to choose them)&quot; That seems like what Im looking for did I miss it?<br /> <br /> I wanted to tentatively start a game soon but unless I can master this I am worried about it...<br /> <br /> The system if GREAT. I'm just tripping over this part.<br /> Thanks in advance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T03:57:35-08:00","id":1189187,"title":"","content":"Hi yrtalien. I\u2019ve seen your question, you\u2019re not being ignored. I\u2019ll try and work through it with you tomorrow. It\u2019s a bit late where I am now to start picking through the system.<br /> <br /> I hope that\u2019s okay with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T05:00:13-08:00","id":1189197,"title":"","content":"Yes, TY so much. I lam enamoured with just about everything about this game and if I can nail this down I will fall completely. I await eagerly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T15:15:34-08:00","id":1189293,"title":"","content":"So I see Ian had a go at answering your question over on rpg.net. Did that make it clearer for you?<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll describe it as I understand it here, noting that I had nothing to do with writing those parts of the rules, so if I get something wrong, someone please feel free to correct me.<br /> <br /> To start: every player character has at least three Injury Condition boxes. These are much like the health boxes of WoD/CofD, but a little different. <br /> <br /> The three Injury Condition boxes are Bruised, Injured, and Maimed. If you have Stamina 3 or 4, you get an additional Injured box. If you have Stamina 5, you get an additional Bruised. Other powers or Gifts might provide more.<br /> <br /> For the sake of this post, let\u2019s call them B, I and M.<br /> <br /> Most characters; [B] [I] [M]<br /> Stamina 3-4: [B] [I] [I] [M]<br /> Stamina 5: [B] [B] [I] [I] [M]<br /> <br /> As these boxes are marked, they impose a Complication of Bruised -1, Inured -2, and Maimed -4. I\u2019ll explain these more in a moment.<br /> <br /> When someone attacks you and chooses the Inflict Damage stunt, you have to mark off one of your boxes. You can\u2019t mark one that\u2019s already marked, and chances are you\u2019re going to choose the one with the lowest Complication. You don\u2019t have to, and some injuries (such as from certain Psi powers) bypass lower Injury Conditions and go straight for the nasty ones.<br /> <br /> This is where some of the narrative elements of Storypath come in. When you mark an Injury Condition box, you choose a way to describe what the Complication is. Using the examples in the text, a Bruised (-1) complication might be bruised ribs, a sprained ankle, or a black eye. The catch with these is that they should fit the scenario, and your Storyguide should agree. So if you\u2019re shot with a pistol and take a Bruised condition, you might adapt \u2018bruised ribs\u2019 to \u2018grazed ribs\u2019, and have it apply to defense actions. The descriptor helps to understand when the complication should apply, and I\u2019m sure you\u2019ve all noticed that not all situations are equal. That\u2019s why you need your Storyguide to agree.<br /> <br /> (By the way, I know that the -1,-2,-4 terminology for Injury Conditions is a bit misleading, since each one imposes a +1/2/4 Complication that requires more successes to overcome. You don\u2019t lose dice from your dice pool.)<br /> <br /> Now, if you\u2019ve taken several Injury Conditions, you only apply the most severe Complication to any roll. For example, if you have a black eye (Bruised -1) and a broken leg (Injured -2), if you\u2019re sitting on a chair and taking a shot with a rifle, you\u2019d only suffer the -1, because you\u2019re not trying to use your leg. If you\u2019re trying to climb a fence, you\u2019d suffer the -2, because your leg is definitely involved. If you\u2019re lunging to catch a grenade and throw it back before it explodes, the Storyguide might say that both black eye and broken leg are relevant, but here you only suffer -2 because that\u2019s the highest.<br /> <br /> In my opinion - when in doubt, apply the complication. You are injured after all.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense, and have I answered the confusion? Are there any follow-on questions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T15:55:51-08:00","id":1189301,"title":"","content":"Bunyip, thanks for this. Now I know you weren't explainjig it for me but the whole health system of the White Wolf etc fame lines have a always casused me issue. (I have always wished it was more hit point then the way it is). <br /> <br /> But this helps to begin clearing it up for me. The whole damage, health, and gralinv isn't fully understand (for all that everything else is) but it's a start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T20:52:56-08:00","id":1189338,"title":"","content":"Bunyip, Thank you, Thank you. Yes, that clears it all up. I'm sorry if I was bothersome. Twenty times Thank you. No more questions on this topic... Though if you've a mind can you tell me what Vitality is? I'm assuming another word for Stamina. Since it is counted towards how much bio-tech you can format... even if can't tell me TY one last time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T21:22:23-08:00","id":1189341,"title":"","content":"Yes, Vitality = Stamina. The terminology for different attributes changed back and forth while we were writing, and some old references didn\u2019t get caught. I\u2019ll make a note to point it out, but if any more slip through we\u2019ll catch them in editing and proof reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T22:12:21-08:00","id":1189346,"title":"","content":"Bunyip, u da mannn!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"M